[{"text":"Contract[expr] contracts pairs of Lorentz or Cartesian indices of metric tensors, vectors and (depending on the value of the option EpsContract) of Levi-Civita tensors in expr.","anchor":"contract"},{"text":"For contractions of Dirac matrices with each other use DiracSimplify.","anchor":"contract"},{"text":"Contract[exp1, exp2] contracts (exp1*exp2), where exp1 and exp2 may be larger products of sums of metric tensors and 4-vectors. This can be also useful when evaluating polarization sums, where exp2 should be the product (or expanded sum) of the polarization sums for the vector bosons.","anchor":"contract"},{"text":"Overview, Pair, CartesianPair, DiracSimplify, MomentumCombine.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"MT[\\[Mu], \\[Nu]] FV[p, \\[Mu]] Contract[%]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\mu } \\bar{g}^{\\mu \\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FV[p, \\[Mu]] GA[\\[Mu]] Contract[%]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\mu } \\overline{p}^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"The default dimension for a metric tensor is 4.","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"MT[\\[Mu], \\[Mu]] Contract[%]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{g}^{\\mu \\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[4\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"A quick way to enter \\(D\\)-dimensional metric tensors is given by MTD.","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"MTD[\\[Mu], \\[Nu]] MTD[\\[Mu], \\[Nu]] Contract[%]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[(g^{\\mu \\nu})^2\\]","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[D\\]","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FV[p, \\[Mu]] FV[q, \\[Mu]] Contract[% ]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\mu } \\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FV[p - q, \\[Mu]] FV[a - b, \\[Mu]] Contract[%]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\left(\\overline{a}-\\overline{b}\\right)^{\\mu } \\left(\\overline{p}-\\overline{q}\\right)^{\\mu }","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{a}\\cdot \\overline{p}-\\overline{a}\\cdot \\overline{q}-\\overline{b}\\cdot \\overline{p}+\\overline{b}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FVD[p - q, \\[Nu]] FVD[a - b, \\[Nu]] Contract[%]","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[(a-b)^{\\nu } (p-q)^{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[a\\cdot p-a\\cdot q-b\\cdot p+b\\cdot q\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"LC[\\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Alpha], \\[Sigma]] FV[p, \\[Sigma]] Contract[%]","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\sigma } \\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\alpha \\sigma }\\]","anchor":"cb8-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\alpha \\mu \\nu \\overline{p}}\\]","anchor":"cb8-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"LC[\\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Alpha], \\[Beta]] LC[\\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Alpha], \\[Sigma]] Contract[%]","anchor":"cb9","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\alpha \\beta } \\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\alpha \\sigma }\\]","anchor":"cb9-3","section":"Examples"}]